  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\theta \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$ and $t_1=(\\tan \\theta)^{\\tan \\theta}, t_2=(\\tan \\theta)^{\\cot \\theta}$ and $t_4=(\\cot \\theta)^{\\tan \\theta}$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "83ao5",
      "text": "\n$t_1>t_2>t_3>t_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ynJpv",
      "text": "\n$t_4>t_3>t_1>t_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Pi08d",
      "text": "\n$t_3>t_1>t_2>t_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Y3JaU",
      "text": "\n$t_2>t_3>t_1>t_4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As when $\\theta \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$\n$\\tan \\theta < \\cot \\theta$\nSince, $\\tan \\theta < 1$ and $\\cot \\theta>1$\n$\\therefore(\\tan \\theta)^{\\cot \\theta} < 1$ and $(\\cot \\theta)^{\\tan \\theta}>1$\n$\\therefore t_4>t_1$ which only holds in option (b).",
    "image": null
  },
